{"id":"resp_b98c1642e20f4ea8","created_at":1795550751,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_804cd12065037f42","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce JSON matching expected_response_schema.\n\nWe must review candidate SHACL against source/schema etc.\n\nWe have candidate version 2 SHACL. Compare to previous version 1. Differences:\n\n- In previous, ex:QuantityShape had sh:targetObjectsOf ... now removed targetObjectsOf. So removal of targetObjectsOf statements: two statements removed. Also add sh:targetClass? Actually now ex:ShipShape has sh:targetClass vocab:ship (same as before). In QuantityShape: previous had targetObjectsOf plus property constraints. New removed targetObjectsOf (the targetObjectsOf lines). That's a change. Also perhaps changed ordering but not semantics.\n\nSo there is a change: removal of sh:targetObjectsOf statements. That's a removal of target constraints, which may affect validation. According to policy, removal of restrictions may be allowed if source-backed excessive restriction. Need to assess if removal is supported by source evidence. The source likely says QuantityShape should target objects of classificationSocietyRuleLength and ruleLength. Did we have evidence? In source evidence, maybe statements about target objects? Not clear. The source likely indicates that QuantityShape is for QUDT QuantityValue used for rule lengths. There may be targetObjectsOf from schema? In the schema terms, there is \"quantityEncoding\" indicating QUDT QuantityValue shape, but not explicit target. Probably the removal is not supported by source. So this could be an issue: removal of targetObjectsOf constraints is a regression (less strict). So we need to report change assessment with removal_disposition possibly UNRESOLVED or REGRESSION if not supported. According to spec, removal_required true for each change? The change_manifest indicates removal_required true for change e91... So must assess removal. Since removal is not source-backed, we should mark disposition as REGRESSION maybe? Let's see schema: change_assessments entries require removal_disposition: SUPPORTED_REMOVAL, REPLACED, REGRESSION, UNRESOLVED. Since removal not approved, we set REGRESSION.\n\nWill need source evidence supporting original targetObjectsOf? Might be in schema: The previous SHACL targetObjectsOf referencing vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength. That aligns with requirement TRF-035 about ruleLength property. Probably source indicates that those properties are QuantityProperty and should be validated.\n\nThus removal not supported. So change assessment: disposition SUPPORTED? No, removal not supported, so REGRESSION.\n\nWe need to provide source_evidence_id and source_excerpt showing original targetObjectsOf? Maybe from previous candidate (old SHACL) but not in evidence. But we can use source evidence that these properties are of type QuantityProperty: evidence E62 etc. There is evidence about ruleLength being QuantityProperty. That could support requirement to target those. So we can cite one of those.\n\nProvide candidate_location: need to locate removal lines in candidate (new) where targetObjectsOf are missing. Since removal, we need previous_location referencing previous candidate lines. Need to compute line numbers: We don't have line numbers but we can approximate. Let's compute lines of previous candidate where targetObjectsOf appear.\n\nPrevious full_code: after ex:QuantityShape a sh:NodeShape ; then sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength ; then blank line ; then sh:property... So targetObjectsOf lines likely line numbers... Let's count quickly.\n\nI'll count lines:\n\n1 @prefix sh...\n2 @prefix rdf...\n3 @prefix rdfs...\n4 @prefix xsd...\n5 @prefix qudt...\n6 @prefix vocab...\n7 @prefix ex...\n8 @prefix unit...\n9 blank?\n10 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n11 # Shape that validates any QUDT...\n12 # -----------------------------------------------------------------\n13 ex:QuantityShape\n14     a sh:NodeShape ;\n15     sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength ;\n16 \n17     # The quantity must have a numeric value (decimal)\n18     sh:property [\n19         sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n20         sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n21         sh:minCount 1 ;\n22         sh:maxCount 1 ;\n23     ] ;\n24     # The quantity must be expressed in metres\n25     sh:property [\n26         sh:path qudt:unit ;\n27         sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n28         sh:minCount 1 ;\n29         sh:maxCount 1 ;\n30     ] .\n...\nShipShape lines later.\n\nThus previous targetObjectsOf line is 15. New candidate lacks that. So removal previous_location line 15 (perhaps unit lines). candidate_location? Since removed, candidate location maybe line where removal occurs? For removal we still give candidate_location (where change is reflected) maybe where the removal is: after line 14? Hard.\n\nSpec: candidate_location for change assessment is location in candidate where change is (added/modified/removed). For removal, we can give location where removal was (i.e., location of previous statement). Use characters lines? We'll approximate with lines = 14-15? Provide start line 14, end line 15.\n\nCandidate SHA256 same.\n\nNow issues array: Since removal results in regression, we need to create issue entry? The spec expects issues describing problems. Could issue be about missing targetObjectsOf causing insufficient validation? Category SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR. Provide source_clause maybe \"sh:targetObjectsOf\". source_evidence_id E62 (ruleLength as QuantityProperty) etc. Provide source_excerpt.\n\nWe need to include issue with change_id referencing the change. Provide expected maybe \"ex:QuantityShape should target ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength\". suggestion: \"Add sh:targetObjectsOf statements as in previous version\". evidence_id perhaps same as source evidence? Provide evidence_id maybe none? Must include evidence_id and evidence_excerpt (engine diagnostics). We have execution_probe with diagnostics stdout empty. So evidence_id could be some generated? maybe we can reference execution diagnostics as evidence? Not required? Must include evidence_id and evidence_excerpt non-empty. Could use captured stdout (empty) but need non-empty substring. Could use a placeholder? But must be exact non-empty substring of that evidence. We have no evidence with text. Could use source evidence as evidence_id? No, evidence_id fields refer to evidence in catalog? The schema defines evidence_id field expected to be an identifier for evidence used to support issue. Could be an RDF fact evidence ID like E62. Provide evidence_excerpt as the exact triple text.\n\nThus for issue, we can set evidence_id \"E62\" and evidence_excerpt the triple as in evidence catalog: \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ruleLength> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#quantityKindLabel> \\\"Length\\\"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string> .\"\n\nSource_evidence_id probably also same? Actually source_evidence_id must identify a SOURCE entry. For source clause \"sh:targetObjectsOf vocab:classificationSocietyRuleLength , vocab:ruleLength ;\" the source might be source entry indicating that these properties are QUDT QuantityValue. Maybe use source evidence like E62 (ruleLength quantity) and E10 (classificationSocietyRuleLength label). We'll pick one source evidence that mentions classificationSocietyRuleLength is a property. Use E10: label. That is source evidence ID \"E10\". Provide source_excerpt that triple.\n\nThus issue: issue_id \"issue-1\". Category SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR.\n\nNow change_assessments: one entry with change_id as in change_manifest e91... Provide disposition \"REGRESSION\". source_evidence_id maybe \"E10\" and \"E62\". source_excerpt maybe same. candidate_location